2. Create the actual page or pages with fake forms on your website or blog; 3. Obtain images, scripts and videos to make your page more realistic, using stock photography if needed; 4 Make sure that the host server is secure and PCI compliant for storing card data; 5 Secure all forms input points with best practice input validation techniques; 6 Add antivirus protection scanning to detect malicious code insertions by hackers;7 Test the page after finalizing every step for functionality and accuracy of data capture – use dummy data instead of real ones if needed;
8 Publish your page using SSL security protocol so all content exchanged between browser user/classmate & your webpage will remain private & securely encrypted 9 Continue updating it regularly with new tricks and tactics used in phishing campaigns -this makes it hard for classmates to stay ahead of you!

